{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And Moses stood in the gate of the camp\"</b> is connected to what was said, for since he saw that the people would become a byword and a taunt among their enemies, and this is a profanation of HaShem's name, he stood in the gate of the camp and called with a loud voice, <b>\"Whoever is for HaShem, to me,\"</b> and killed publicly all the worshippers of the calf, so that the matter would be heard among them, and the name of Heaven would be sanctified through them in place of the profanation they had committed."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:24.169343454Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}